        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>OLED monitors are all the rage for PC gamers at the moment, especially those who have a little discretionary spending available. Most of the panels in those monitors\u2014whatever the brand on the label\u2014come from either LG or Samsung\u2026 and the latter just unveiled a new panel that\u2019ll turn heads: the first 32-inch 4K OLED with 360Hz speed.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>There have been plenty of 32-inch 4K OLEDs in the last few years, but they max out at 240Hz or have to <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2876158/asus-rog-strix-oled-xg32ucwg-review.html\">bump the resolution down to go faster</a>. Samsung\u2019s Display division says that this new QD-OLED panel announced at Computex 2026 can pull that trick too, stepping down to 1080p resolution to go into overdrive at 680Hz. Dang. Other features include VESA DisplayHDR True Black 600 certification and a V-stripe pixel structure for c",
